---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Security — Camvella HOA Management Software"
  description="How Camvella protects management-company and association data with tenant isolation, role-based access, private storage, encryption, auditability, and controlled infrastructure access."
>
  <div style="padding-top:64px;background:var(--clr-navy);color:white">
    <div class="container" style="padding-top:var(--space-20);padding-bottom:var(--space-16);max-width:900px">
      <p class="section__label" style="color:var(--clr-amber-light)">Security & trust</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.4rem,4vw,3.6rem);line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">Association data should stay with the association it belongs to.</h1>
      <p style="font-size:var(--text-lg);color:rgba(255 255 255/.72);max-width:65ch;line-height:1.7">Camvella is designed around management-company and association separation, role-based access, private files, encrypted transport, and database-level tenant controls. We document implemented controls without claiming certifications we have not independently verified.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section__label">Core controls</p>
      <h2 class="section__headline">Security built around multi-community operations.</h2>
      <div class="security-grid">
        <article><h3>Database-enforced isolation</h3><p>Organization and association access is enforced with PostgreSQL Row Level Security so one management company cannot query another company’s records through ordinary application access.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Role-based permissions</h3><p>Operational and financial access is separated by role so managers, accounting staff, board users, residents, auditors, and support roles receive only the access required for their work.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Private document storage</h3><p>Association and customer files are designed for private storage and controlled access rather than permanent public URLs.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Financial auditability</h3><p>Financial workflows are designed around immutable or traceable records, controlled period changes, reversals, and audit-oriented access rather than silent history replacement.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Encrypted transport</h3><p>HTTPS is enforced across Camvella domains and traffic is protected in transit with modern TLS through Cloudflare and the managed application stack.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Privileged access boundaries</h3><p>Service credentials and backend secrets stay server-side. Customer-facing users do not receive infrastructure credentials or broad database access.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section__label">What buyers should ask</p>
      <h2 class="section__headline">A security review should go beyond the vendor logo list.</h2>
      <div class="buyer-grid">
        <article><strong>Can another portfolio see my communities?</strong><span>Tenant and association boundaries are enforced at the database layer.</span></article>
        <article><strong>Can board or resident users see accounting they should not?</strong><span>Permissions are role-aware and scoped to the appropriate association and workflow.</span></article>
        <article><strong>Are documents public?</strong><span>Sensitive files are designed for private storage and controlled access.</span></article>
        <article><strong>Can changes be traced?</strong><span>Financial and sensitive workflows are built with auditability and controlled changes in mind.</span></article>
        <article><strong>Who can access production?</strong><span>Privileged infrastructure access is restricted and service credentials are not exposed to customer users.</span></article>
        <article><strong>What certifications do you have?</strong><span>Camvella does not advertise SOC 2, ISO 27001, or other certifications unless independently verified for the specific scope.</span></article>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:var(--space-10);display:flex;gap:var(--space-3);flex-wrap:wrap">
        <a href="/demo" class="btn btn--primary btn--lg">Book a security walkthrough</a>
        <a href="/privacy" class="btn btn--dark btn--lg">Read privacy policy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.security-grid,.buyer-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px;margin-top:32px}
.security-grid article,.buyer-grid article{padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--clr-border);border-radius:16px;background:#fff}
.security-grid h3,.buyer-grid strong{display:block;color:var(--clr-navy);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:10px}
.security-grid p,.buyer-grid span{display:block;color:var(--clr-text-soft);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.68}
@media(max-width:900px){.security-grid,.buyer-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
@media(max-width:620px){.security-grid,.buyer-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
